{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["<b>I too will do this to you.</b> Measure for measure. I said, ״and it shall be if you indeed listen,״ etc. — ״I will put no disease upon you, for I am HaShem your healer.״ Now, if you do not listen to Me, I am not your healer but will visit upon you evil illnesses." "<b>Behalah.</b> Corresponding to ״you shall dwell, and nothing shall terrify״ — now there is terror." "<b>Behalah et the shachefet.</b> Etc. Behalah of shachefet (consumption) and of fever, which consume the eyes — they hope for a remedy but there is none. Another interpretation: <b>et the shachefet</b> — together with the shachefet. Rashi explained: and which is this? A blow of death. Some interpret it as meaning waiting — prolonged expectation that does not arrive. One may say: a blow of the lower back, and it is the first blow." "<b>And wasting of soul.</b> Corresponding to ״that they should be servants״ — that is, I took you out from the misery of servitude on condition that you accept and fulfill My commandments; now that you have not fulfilled them, I will visit upon you misery of soul, and it is the second blow." "<b>And you shall sow in vain.</b> Your seed — corresponding to ״and it shall yield to you threshing״ — and it is the third blow." "<b>And your enemies shall eat it.</b> Counterpart to 'and you shall eat': I said that you shall eat; now your enemies shall eat it. And this is the fourth blow."], :book :leviticus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 26, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:15:36.664163540Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}